WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.294
Welcome to Go Live, your final step in preparing for route operations.

2
00:00:06.294 --> 00:00:12.588
This lesson should only be started once your practice route is complete.

3
00:00:12.588 --> 00:00:18.881
The system calculates readiness based on your organization's records, training progress, route status, and proof evidence.

4
00:00:18.881 --> 00:00:25.175
Remember, a checked box in the browser isn't a substitute for persisted workspace facts.

5
00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:31.813
First, confirm your training evidence.

6
00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:38.450
The Customer Champion must complete 'Start Here', 'Workspace Setup', 'Route Operations', and this 'Go Live' track with passing knowledge checks.

7
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:45.088
Ensure at least one Driver role team member has completed 'Driver Quick Start'.

8
00:00:45.088 --> 00:00:51.725
Verify that the selected Champion is still responsible for preparation, internal follow-through, and customer signoff.

9
00:00:51.725 --> 00:01:01.033
Next, confirm your operating evidence.

10
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:10.342
Your organization needs a primary depot, active Driver, ready vehicle, imported jobs, validated locations, provider-backed route, dispatched practice route, and persisted proof.

11
00:01:10.342 --> 00:01:19.650
If any step is incomplete, open the readiness card action to resolve the underlying record, rather than asking Support to mark it complete manually.

12
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:25.730
Rehearse the support and exception path.

13
00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:31.810
The Driver records on-road conditions and messages Dispatch.

14
00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:37.890
The Dispatcher owns route changes and customer impact coordination.

15
00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:43.970
The Champion owns access, policy, privacy, and escalation issues.

16
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:50.050
Preserve record identifiers and request IDs, but never share passwords, tokens, access codes, or unnecessary customer data with support.

17
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:58.592
Prepare for the first month review.

18
00:01:58.592 --> 00:02:07.133
Record the baseline and assign an owner for planning time, planned and actual mileage, unassigned jobs, late risk stops, failed deliveries, proof completion, Driver and Dispatcher support questions, and knowledge base searches without a useful answer.

19
00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:15.675
Review these measures after week one and again on day thirty.

20
00:02:15.675 --> 00:02:22.138
Acknowledge your customer responsibilities and submit the final knowledge check.

21
00:02:22.138 --> 00:02:28.600
Once every training and operational step is complete, the readiness card will say 'Ready for Review'.

22
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:35.063
Use the included thirty-minute checkpoint to confirm remaining blockers, escalation ownership, fallback procedures, and the exact launch date.

23
00:02:35.063 --> 00:02:41.525
This isn't a replacement for the Academy.

24
00:02:41.525 --> 00:02:49.800
Finally, compare the Academy readiness card with the signed docket.

25
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:58.075
The same Champion, trained pilot Driver, route evidence, proof, escalation owner, and KPI dates should appear in both.

26
00:02:58.075 --> 00:03:06.350
Write down any remaining blockers and their owners before booking the checkpoint.

27
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:14.625
When the card is green, schedule the single readiness review with the people who can make launch decisions, then keep broader team questions in the searchable Academy and support hub.
